{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793178391,"nonce":"1NAVqE+DXKMXcLrgg25k0pBobiw=","title":"Release publisher has an invalid crate set and can report success after failures","message":"Read-only release audit of scripts/publish-crates.sh on 183186b2:\n- blinc_layout depends on blinc_css, but the publisher never publishes blinc_css.\n- blinc_runtime, blinc_test_suite and blinc_debugger set publish=false, yet appear in its phase arrays.\n- blinc_canvas_kit lives in excluded, gitignored packages/, so root cargo publish -p cannot select it.\n- publish_phase calls publish_crate in an if with no failure branch, swallowing failed crates and continuing later phases. The final success message is then misleading.\n- publish_crate ignores cargo exit status and infers success from output keywords.\n- Every publish uses --no-verify. No explicit nonpublishing plan/preflight mode exists.\n\nRepair before release: derive or validate a publishable crate set and dependency order from metadata, include required CSS, fail on the real Cargo status, and provide reviewable nonpublishing plan and dry-run behavior. Do not publish as part of this repair. Existing release version/API compatibility and hosted CI on local commits require separate review.","files":null}]}